#### 3. Automated Fulfillment Dispatchers for Detected Bounties
Implement specialized solvers in `scripts/` to capture detected rewards:
- **For Item #1602563** (*"Show Your Build Weekly #7: Post Your Proof-of-Work 🔨"* in `~Construction_and_Engineering`):
  Create [`scripts/sn_build_solver.mjs`](file:///scripts/sn_build_solver.mjs) that formats a technical Proof-of-Work submission showcasing the open-source automation architecture of `relayhop/sn-monetization-runtime`, including repository architecture links, live benchmark metrics, and Lightning invoice to claim the 5,000 sat reward.
- **For Item #1601866** (*"Stacker Stocks Weekly Close Contest 🟩 or 🟥"* in `~Stacker_Stocks`):
  Create [`scripts/sn_contest_solver.mjs`](file:///scripts/sn_contest_solver.mjs) that fetches the target stock index price, calculates sentiment momentum, formats the binary prediction comment (🟩 Green or 🟥 Red) with payout invoice, and claims the 10,000–20,000 sat bounty.

---

### What alternative solutions did you explore? (Optional)

1. **GitHub Issues Search API (`octokit.rest.search.issuesAndPullRequests`)**:
   - *Exploration*: Dynamically searching GitHub issues on every workflow run using `q: repo:owner/repo is:issue is:open label:bounty ...`.
   - *Drawback*: The GitHub Search API enforces a strict secondary rate limit of 30 requests/minute and has a search indexing delay of 10–60 seconds. In overlapping cron runs, index latency allows race conditions where two workflows query GitHub before the first issue is indexed, opening duplicates like #1338 and #1339.
   - *Selected approach*: Maintaining a Git-tracked persistent file (`data/sn_targets_accumulated/alerted_bounties.tsv`) provides atomic, local, zero-API-cost deduplication, with `issues.listForRepo` serving as a resilient secondary defense.

2. **Single Pinned Living Dashboard Issue**:
   - *Exploration*: Updating a single pinned issue with an active table of currently open bounties instead of creating individual issues.
   - *Drawback*: Eliminates individual issue discussions, per-bounty PR referencing, webhook automation triggers, and milestone tracking. Retaining deterministic, ID-keyed issues (`[sn-${id}]`) provides complete traceability while completely eliminating spam.

3. **GitHub Actions Cache (`actions/cache`)**:
   - *Exploration*: Caching the alerted bounty ID list via GitHub Actions cache across runs.
   - *Trade-off*: GitHub Actions caches are subject to eviction policies, branch isolation restrictions, and eventual consistency delays. Storing the ledger in Git-persisted storage guarantees permanent persistence and auditable commit history.

---

### What automated tests can you add to prevent this from re-occurring?

Add a comprehensive unit test suite in [`tests/sn_radar_dedup.test.mjs`](file:///tests/sn_radar_dedup.test.mjs) using Node.js built-in test runner (`node --test`):

```javascript
import { test, describe, beforeEach, afterEach } from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import os from 'node:os';

describe('Stacker News Radar Bounty Deduplication Suite', () => {
  let tmpDir;
  let ledgerPath;

  beforeEach(() => {
    tmpDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'sn-radar-dedup-test-'));
    ledgerPath = path.join(tmpDir, 'alerted_bounties.tsv');
  });

  afterEach(() => {
    fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });
  });

  // Deduplication core logic handler
  function filterNewBounties(ledgerFile, incomingRows) {
    const seen = new Set();
    if (fs.existsSync(ledgerFile)) {
      const lines = fs.readFileSync(ledgerFile, 'utf8').split('\n');
      for (const line of lines) {
        if (!line.trim() || line.startsWith('#')) continue;
        const cols = line.split('\t');
        if (cols[1]) seen.add(cols[1].trim());
      }
    } else {
      fs.writeFileSync(ledgerFile, '# discovered_at\tid\tsub\ttier\tscore\tbounty\n');
    }

    const newRows = [];
    for (const row of incomingRows) {
      const cols = row.split('\t');
      const id = cols[0];
      if (id && !seen.has(id)) {
        newRows.push(row);
        seen.add(id);
        fs.appendFileSync(ledgerFile, `${new Date().toISOString()}\t${row}\n`);
      }
    }
    return newRows;
  }

  test('correctly records and alerts newly discovered bounties on first detection', () => {
    const bountyConstruction = '1602563\tConstruction_and_Engineering\t2\t141\t5000\t1\t9.5\t9274\t28948\ttop@Construction_and_Engineering\tOPEN_BOUNTY,LOW_COMP,SIGNAL\tShow Your Build Weekly #7';
    const bountyStocks = '1601866\tStacker_Stocks\t2\t319\t10000\t26\t35.6\t9274\t28948\trecent@Stacker_Stocks\tOPEN_BOUNTY\tStacker Stocks Weekly Close Contest';

    const newItems = filterNewBounties(ledgerPath, [bountyConstruction, bountyStocks]);

    assert.equal(newItems.length, 2);
    assert.equal(newItems[0].split('\t')[0], '1602563');
    assert.equal(newItems[1].split('\t')[0], '1601866');
    assert.ok(fs.existsSync(ledgerPath));
  });

  test('strictly rejects duplicate bounty on subsequent cron executions', () => {
    const bountyStocks = '1601866\tStacker_Stocks\t2\t319\t10000\t26\t35.6\t9274\t28948\trecent@Stacker_Stocks\tOPEN_BOUNTY\tStacker Stocks Weekly Close Contest';

    // First execution
    const run1 = filterNewBounties(ledgerPath, [bountyStocks]);
    assert.equal(run1.length, 1);

    // Second execution (simulating next cron run or overlapping workflow)
    const run2 = filterNewBounties(ledgerPath, [bountyStocks]);
    assert.equal(run2.length, 0, 'Must strictly suppress previously alerted active bounty');

    // Third execution across multi-hour scheduling
    const run3 = filterNewBounties(ledgerPath, [bountyStocks]);
    assert.equal(run3.length, 0, 'Must suppress repeating open bounties across all cron intervals');
  });

  test('allows new independent bounty ID while suppressing existing persistent bounty', () => {
    const existingBounty = '1601866\tStacker_Stocks\t2\t319\t10000\t26\t35.6\t9274\t28948\trecent@Stacker_Stocks\tOPEN_BOUNTY\tStacker Stocks Weekly Close Contest';
    const newBounty = '1602563\tConstruction_and_Engineering\t2\t141\t5000\t1\t9.5\t9274\t28948\ttop@Construction_and_Engineering\tOPEN_BOUNTY\tShow Your Build Weekly #7';

    // Seed existing bounty
    filterNewBounties(ledgerPath, [existingBounty]);

    // Ingest both together (as in Issue #1341)
    const mixedRun = filterNewBounties(ledgerPath, [existingBounty, newBounty]);
    assert.equal(mixedRun.length, 1, 'Only the unalerted bounty must pass through');
    assert.equal(mixedRun[0].split('\t')[0], '1602563', 'Newly discovered item #1602563 must be selected');
  });

  test('deterministic title tag generator formats unique search keys', () => {
    const id = '1602563';
    const title = 'Show Your Build Weekly #7';
    const bounty = '5000';
    const formatted = `[radar] SN bounty #${id} [sn-${id}]: ${title} (${bounty} Sats)`;

    assert.ok(formatted.includes(`[sn-${id}]`));
    assert.match(formatted, /\[sn-1602563\]/);
  });
});
```

